<!--
  regression-extention-retenue.dtd : the contract for lib/regression.mjs.

  Three words, three questions, in the order a release must ask them.

    REGRESSION  what left between two tags, and was a reason recorded
    EXTENTION   what arrived, and is anything reading it
    RETENUE     what stayed with no reader, and is the reason it is kept
                written down

  Written after the v7.0.0 hunt that found nothing. A diff-based detector
  would have returned green on that release, because v6.0.0..v7.0.0 deleted
  no file at all: the only regression was a COMMENT that claimed the Adiutor
  read RECORD.info. Pass 13 invented that reader, pass 14 named 13's reader
  as nonexistent and invented a second, pass 15 wrote the truth. Three
  passes, two hallucinated capabilities, and every one of them would have
  passed a diff.

  So the instrument reads CLAIMS, not diffs. LAW.RER.2 is the whole reason
  this file exists: a comment that says something reads X is checked against
  the thing it names, and a reader that does not contain X is a finding.

  This subset uses a conditional section on purpose. lib/dtd.mjs has carried
  flattenConditionals() since before 7.0.0 and no file in dtd/ ever used it;
  a resolver nobody exercises is the same defect class this file hunts, so
  the hunt begins with its own tooling.
-->

<!ENTITY % rer.strict "INCLUDE">

<!ELEMENT regression_run (scope, finding*, verdict)>
<!ATTLIST regression_run
          from CDATA #REQUIRED
          to   CDATA #REQUIRED>

<!ELEMENT scope (#PCDATA)>
<!ATTLIST scope
          files    CDATA #REQUIRED
          removed  CDATA #REQUIRED
          arrived  CDATA #REQUIRED>

<!-- One finding. `kind` is which of the three questions it answers.
     `subject` is the declaration, entity or capability it is about.
     `where` is the file and line it was read from, so a reader can argue. -->
<!ELEMENT finding (#PCDATA)>
<!ATTLIST finding
          kind       (regression|extention|retenue) #REQUIRED
          subject    CDATA #REQUIRED
          where      CDATA #REQUIRED
          severity   (high|medium|low) #REQUIRED
          confidence (measured|reasoned|guessed) #REQUIRED>

<!ELEMENT verdict EMPTY>
<!ATTLIST verdict
          value    (clean|findings) #REQUIRED
          findings CDATA #REQUIRED>

<!ENTITY RER.verdict.clean    "REGRESSION VERDICT: clean">
<!ENTITY RER.verdict.findings "REGRESSION VERDICT: findings">

<!-- The shapes a capability claim takes in a comment. A claim names a
     reader and a subject; the reader is a path or a module name this
     repository can open. -->
<!ENTITY RER.claim.reads   "a comment saying that some named thing reads, checks or consumes a named declaration">
<!ENTITY RER.claim.reader  "the file the claim names, which must exist and must contain the subject">
<!ENTITY RER.vestigial     "a declaration that survives with no reader and carries the reason it is kept">

<![ %rer.strict; [
<!-- Strict: a claim whose reader cannot be opened is a high finding rather
     than a note. Set rer.strict to IGNORE before the include to downgrade
     every claim finding to low, which is what a survey run wants. -->
<!ENTITY RER.claim.unresolved.severity "high">
]]>

<!ENTITY LAW.RER.1 "Every declaration that left the tree between the two tags is listed with the commit that removed it and the reason recorded in that commit body; a removal whose commit body does not mention it is a regression finding, and a release that deleted no file still runs this arm because a declaration can leave a file that stays.">
<!ENTITY LAW.RER.2 "A capability a comment asserts is checked against the reader it names: the claim RER.claim.reads must resolve to RER.claim.reader, that file must exist, and it must contain the subject; a claim naming a reader that does not contain the subject is a finding of kind regression at RER.claim.unresolved.severity, because a comment is documentation and a wrong one is a defect that ships.">
<!ENTITY LAW.RER.3 "Retenue: a declaration that survives with no reader anywhere is reported as RER.vestigial, and it is a finding only when no comment within the twelve lines above it gives the reason it is kept; RECORD.info is the reference case and its recorded reason is that the parameter entity command-info-types needs a reference.">
<!ENTITY LAW.RER.4 "A mechanic this codebase implements and never exercises is a retenue finding of its own: code that no caller reaches cannot be trusted when a release finally reaches it, and flattenConditionals in lib/dtd.mjs is the case that named this law.">
<!ENTITY LAW.RER.5 "The run ends with exactly one verdict line, RER.verdict.clean or RER.verdict.findings, and a verdict of findings carries the count; a run that names findings and then reports clean is a broken instrument and exits 2.">
